This project will use a local Kafka Cluster.

To create and start the cluster, and to add the topic:

1. Ensure WSL is installed on your machine if running on Windows

    - open PowerShell as administrator
    - use command "wsl --install"
    - after installation, restart

2. Install Docker Desktop or Docker Engine

    https://docs.docker.com/desktop/setup/install/windows-install/

3. Verify installation

    docker info

4. Install confluent CLI:

    linux/mac
    brew install confluentinc/tap/cli

    windows
    - download the .zip from https://github.com/confluentinc/cli/releases/latest
    - unzip
    - from command line, run confluent.exe

    see other methods here:
    https://docs.confluent.io/confluent-cli/current/install.html

5. Use the command "confluent local kafka start" in your linux or mac terminal. For windows, add the installation folder
containing confluent.exe to system path, then run the command.

    -this will produce the ports to configure your producers and consumers with

    -example:
        +-----------------+-------+
        | Kafka REST Port | 8082  |
        | Plaintext Ports | 51381 |
        +-----------------+-------+

    - use the plain text port for your classes in the BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS_CONFIG variable

6. run "confluent local kafka topic create purchases" to create the purchases topic used in this application

========================================================================================================================

To install shadowJar:

1. in main director use the command "gradle shadowJar" or run the gradle wrapper "./gradlew shadowJar"

========================================================================================================================

Run "confluent local kafka stop" to stop the cluster.
